      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-242997",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/ae/aeda4dcfdb6fb2fb83fdb02d6d71789c0e86091b7cf83b3137704f2b5883f5c5.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $CB^(\u27f7)\u2225DE^(\u27f7)$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> *The sum of the measures of the interior angles of $\u25b3ABC$ equals $180^{\u2218}$.*\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $CB^(\u27f7)\u2225DE^(\u27f7)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 2 | $m\u2220DAC + m\u2220CAB + m\u2220EAB$<br>$= m\u2220DAE$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 3 | $m\u2220DAE = 180^{\u2218}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 4 | $m\u2220DAC + m\u2220CAB + m\u2220EAB$<br>$= 180^{\u2218}$ | {{field-4}} |\n| 5 | $\u2220DAC\u2245\u2220ACB$ | Alternate interior angles theorem |\n| 6 | $m\u2220DAC = m\u2220ACB$ | {{field-5}} |\n| 7 | $\u2220EAB\u2245\u2220ABC$ | {{field-6}} |\n| 8 | $m\u2220EAB = m\u2220ABC$ | Definition of congruent angles |\n| 9 | $m\u2220ACB + m\u2220CAB + m\u2220ABC$<br>$= 180^{\u2218}$ | {{field-7}} |"
    },
