      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-243007",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/34/349721f8bbb31a2b04fead1f4d5e24e83ed8e3980c4dee0bf9781fe212c1e0d1.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, the points $B$, $C$, and $D$ are colinear.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> $x = y + z$\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $x + m\u2220CAD + m\u2220C = 180^{\u2218}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 2 | $m\u2220BAC = z + m\u2220CAD$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 3 | $y + m\u2220BAC + m\u2220C = 180^{\u2218}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 4 | $y + z + m\u2220CAD + m\u2220C = 180^{\u2218}$ | {{field-4}} |\n| 5 | $180^{\u2218} = y + z + m\u2220CAD + m\u2220C$ | {{field-5}} |\n| 6 | $x + m\u2220CAD + m\u2220C = y + z + m\u2220CAD + m\u2220C$ | {{field-6}} |\n| 7 | $x = y + z$ | {{field-7}} |"
